{"dog":{"age_group":"young","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Domestic Short Hair Cross","breed_primary":"Domestic Short Hair Cross","description_text":"My Foster Wrires:\nLeonardo is a little miracle of healing. His shelter pictures show him when his poor tail was still raw from his nervous habit of pulling out his own fur to deal with a situation - he can't tell me what it was but I hear it included animal, situational and human stressors - that was just too much for him. Now, finally, for the first time in his kitty life, he has space and quiet to himself, and has been able to show me and my friends what a real jewel he is. He starts purring halfway down the hall and will push his furry face into your hand in anticipation of pets. He runs after a ping pong ball as joyously as a little kitten. He's thrilled by the sights and sounds outside the window but is just as happy keeping company on a desktop or next to a good book. He can be content all by himself if that's what is called for, too. It's incredibly rewarding to offer him a place where he can be his best self, and that best self is everything a wonderful cat could ever offer.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=2%2C15&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=8&searchType=4&animalid=202469","id":"bc712eecb40444a82b94ea9568ef87bf","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/0df371de450a48c18e297e6cd6305933-1794842081-1794842090-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/cdd9acfb425f4cb890ef25d7d679b9d5-1790776894-1790776894-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/cc451a879e704228b742c6cde5e74964-1788213097-1788213097-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/688de3eb70354318b6b0e53a32f32d75-1788213096-1788213096-jpg/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/6a33335ce0c44b82ada1a8e